# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree.
#
# Why this exists: `dist/` is committed and `dist/cli.js` is published as the
# `autobiomemory` bin. On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git
# for Windows default) the working tree held CRLF, so a `pnpm run pack:dist`
# from that machine would ship a `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` shebang and every Unix
# install would fail with `bad interpreter`. Pinning `eol=lf` here makes the
# working tree byte-identical on every platform, regardless of `autocrlf`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never rewrite binary payloads while normalising.
*.zstd binary
*.tgz  binary
*.sqlite binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
